$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-32x-28y+30y & = \\\\ -32x+(-28y+30y) & = \\\\ -32x+2y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054380 1074 "First, we distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(5 - y) \\cdot 3 - 10 &=  \\\\\n5 \\cdot 3 + (-y) \\cdot 3 - 10 &=  \\\\\n(15) + (-3y) - 10 &=  \\\\\n&= 15 - 3y - 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n15 - 3y - 10 &=  \\\\\n(15 - 10) - 3y &=  \\\\\n&= 5 - 3y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 17592186045417 false] [17592186054380 1074 "First, we distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-y)\\cdot 3-10 & = \\\\ 5\\cdot 3+(-y)\\cdot 3-10 & = \\\\ (15)+(-3y)-10 & = \\\\ 15-3y-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15-3y-10 & = \\\\ (15-10)-3y & = \\\\ 5-3y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054785 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445776 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054785 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445778 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054786 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445777 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054786 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445779 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054787 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445780 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054787 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445781 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186054888 1050 420.0 13194139534960 17592186045417 true] [17592186056008 1064 "To simplify an expression containing parentheses, we expand the parentheses and then collect like terms.\n\nFor example, let's simplify the following expression:\n\n$$\n3(x + 2) + 4x\n$$\n\nOur first step is to distribute the $3$ over each of the terms in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3(x + 2) + 4x \\\\[5pt] &= 3\\cdot x + 3\\cdot 2 + 4x \\\\[5pt] &= (3x) + (6) + 4x \\\\[5pt] &= 3x +6 + 4x & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second and final step is to collect